  "reply_text": "**Found one merge blocker.**\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` evaluates as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, effectively checking the READ bit instead of WRITE. I reproduced `canEdit({ mask: READ, locked: false }) === true`; a WRITE-only share is incorrectly denied.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Use `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`. Add regression tests for unlocked READ-only, READ|COMMENT, and WRITE-only shares.\n\nAll 6 existing tests pass, but `test/guard.test.js` only tests editing with all editor rights enabled, which hides the bug.\n\nNo other concrete findings. No files changed.",
